    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d843">

                <pb facs="1255" n="1239" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767N.90D/7–2049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Legation in Syria
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-20T19:00:00-04:00">July 20, 1949—7 p.
                        m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>288. Express to Syrian Govt gratification USG
                    with regard signature Israeli-Syrian armistice agreement on July 20<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d843-f1"/> and express hope this further step toward peace in
                    Palestine will increase possibilities successful conclusion to meetings now
                    taking place with PCC at Lausanne.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d843-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d843-f1" n="1" xml:id="d843-f1-content">
                <p>For text, see SC, <hi rendition="#italic">4th yr.,
                        Special Supplement No. 2</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d843-f2" n="2" xml:id="d843-f2-content"> This telegram was sent
                simultaneously, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to Tel Aviv as No.
                461. Nos. 288 and 461 were repeated to New York. <p>For the statement made by
                    Secretary Acheson on July 20 on the signing of the Israeli-Syrian armistice, see
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, August 8, 1949, p.
                    180.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
